Data
├── Asset
│   └── when the vault has a configured underlying token
│       └── it should return the underlying token address
├── TotalAssets
│   ├── when the vault is empty
│   │   └── it should return zero without adding virtual assets
│   └── when the vault holds assets
│       └── it should return only the vault's actual underlying balance
└── ExportSelectors
    └── it should return the packed selectors for asset and totalAssets

ConvertToShares
├── when the asset amount is zero
│   └── it should return zero
├── when the vault is empty
│   └── it should use the virtual asset and share offsets
├── when the vault has assets and shares
│   └── it should return the equivalent shares rounded down
├── when the product exceeds 256 bits but the quotient fits
│   └── it should preserve full precision and round down
└── ExportSelectors
    └── it should return only the packed convertToShares selector

ConvertToAssets
├── when the share amount is zero
│   └── it should return zero
├── when the vault is empty
│   └── it should use the virtual asset and share offsets
├── when the vault has assets and shares
│   └── it should return the equivalent assets rounded down
├── when the product exceeds 256 bits but the quotient fits
│   └── it should preserve full precision and round down
└── ExportSelectors
    └── it should return only the packed convertToAssets selector

Deposit
├── MaxDeposit
│   └── it should return the unlimited deposit limit
├── PreviewDeposit
│   └── it should quote shares rounded down using the virtual offsets
├── when the receiver is zero
│   └── it should revert with the invalid receiver error
├── when the quote is zero, including a positive deposit that rounds to zero
│   └── it should revert without pulling assets
├── when the asset transfer fails or returns malformed data
│   └── it should leave underlying balances, share balances and supply unchanged
├── when the deposit succeeds, including an asset that returns no data
│   └── it should pull the requested assets, mint the quoted shares and emit Transfer and Deposit
└── ExportSelectors
    └── it should return the packed maxDeposit, previewDeposit and deposit selectors

Mint
├── MaxMint
│   └── it should return the unlimited mint limit
├── PreviewMint
│   └── it should quote assets rounded up using the virtual offsets
├── when the receiver is zero or the quote is zero
│   └── it should revert with the corresponding error
├── when the asset transfer fails or returns malformed data
│   └── it should leave underlying balances, share balances and supply unchanged
├── when the mint succeeds, including an asset that returns no data
│   └── it should pull the quoted assets, mint the requested shares and emit Transfer and Deposit
└── ExportSelectors
    └── it should return the packed maxMint, previewMint and mint selectors

Withdraw
├── MaxWithdraw
│   └── it should return the owner's shares converted to assets rounded down
├── PreviewWithdraw
│   └── it should quote shares rounded up using the virtual offsets
├── when the receiver or owner is zero, the request exceeds the maximum, or the quote is zero
│   └── it should revert with the corresponding error
├── when the owner or an approved spender withdraws
│   └── it should burn the quoted shares, pay the requested assets and emit Transfer and Withdraw
└── ExportSelectors
    └── it should return the packed maxWithdraw, previewWithdraw and withdraw selectors

Redeem
├── MaxRedeem
│   └── it should return the owner's share balance
├── PreviewRedeem
│   └── it should quote assets rounded down using the virtual offsets
├── when the receiver or owner is zero, the request exceeds the maximum, or the quote is zero (including positive shares that round down to zero assets)
│   └── it should revert with the corresponding error
├── when the owner or an approved spender redeems
│   └── it should burn the requested shares, pay the quoted assets and emit Transfer and Withdraw
└── ExportSelectors
    └── it should return the packed maxRedeem, previewRedeem and redeem selectors

Withdrawal and redemption authorization
├── when the caller is the owner
│   └── it should not require allowance
├── when a spender has finite allowance
│   └── it should spend the shares burned, or revert if allowance is insufficient
├── when a spender has unlimited allowance
│   └── it should not decrease allowance
├── when the transfer fails or returns malformed data
│   └── it should roll back the share burn and allowance spending
└── when the asset transfers without returning data
    └── it should still pay the receiver

Diamond integration
├── when the facets are installed on one diamond
│   └── it should share the underlying asset and share storage across the routed calls
├── when depositing and redeeming on the diamond
│   └── it should keep data, quotes, balances, supply and asset payouts consistent
├── when the vault receives an asset transfer directly
│   └── it should update totalAssets and quotes without minting shares
├── when the vault receives assets before the first deposit
│   └── it should mint the quoted shares on the first deposit when the quote is positive
├── when minting and withdrawing through an approved spender
│   ├── it should use the share allowance from the installed ERC20 facets
│   └── it should pull assets before minting shares and burn shares before paying assets
├── when two users enter and exit a funded vault at a fractional exchange rate
│   └── it should execute all four actions at their quoted amounts and keep balances and supply consistent
├── when a user deposits and immediately redeems in a funded vault
│   ├── it should not return more assets than the user deposited
│   └── it should quote the same conversions regardless of the caller
└── when the asset observes the vault during a transfer
    ├── it should see the pre-deposit quote before pulling assets
    └── it should see the final withdrawal quote after paying assets
